# Clean Architecture

Feature-first under `lib/src/modules/<feature>/`. Each feature has three layers:

```
modules/<feature>/
├── domain/           # entities, repository contracts, usecases — PURE
├── infrastructure/   # datasources, dtos, mappers, repository impls
└── presentation/     # blocs, pages, widgets, module_routes.dart
```

## Golden rule

`domain` MUST NOT import from `infrastructure` or `presentation`. Dependencies point inward only.

## Layer responsibilities

- **Domain**: immutable entities with `freezed` (NO `json_serializable` here). Repository contracts as `abstract interface class`. UseCases follow base `UseCase<Output, Input>` from `core/usecases/usecase.dart`.
- **Infrastructure**: DataSources do raw I/O and throw `Exception`s. DTOs use `freezed + json_serializable`. Mappers as extension methods (`UserDtoX.toEntity()`). Repository impls catch exceptions and return `Either<AppFailure, T>`. Decide local-vs-remote (offline-first).
- **Presentation**: Blocs depend ONLY on usecases, never repositories. States modeled with `freezed` sealed classes. Pages are dumb (only listen to bloc and render).

## Naming

- Interface: `IAuthRepository` / Impl: `AuthRepository`
- UseCase: `SignInUseCase`, `GetProfileUseCase`
- Bloc: `AuthBloc`, `AuthState`, `AuthEvent` (or Cubit + State for simple flows)
- DTO: `UserDto`; Entity: `User`

## DI annotations

- `@injectable` — new instance per call (usecases)
- `@lazySingleton` — first-call instantiated (repositories, datasources)
- `@singleton` — eager (services like `AppDatabase`, `SupabaseService`)

## Cross-feature code

- `lib/src/core/` — DI, errors (`AppFailure`), network, routing, storage, supabase, base usecase, extensions.
- `lib/src/design_system/` — theme + reusable components.
- `lib/src/app/` — `main.dart`, `bootstrap.dart`, `app_widget.dart`, environment config.
